       --cc _c_h_d_i_r_-_p_a_t_h
              Sets the current directory used by _b_o_o_t_p_e_f while creating exten‐
              sion  files.   This  is useful when the extension file names are
              specified as relative pathnames, and _b_o_o_t_p_e_f needs  to  use  the
              same current directory as the TFTP server (typically /tftpboot).

       --dd _d_e_b_u_g_-_l_e_v_e_l
              Sets the _d_e_b_u_g_-_l_e_v_e_l variable that controls the amount of debug‐
              ging  messages generated.  For example, ‐d4 or ‐d 4 will set the
              debugging level to 4.

       --ff _c_o_n_f_i_g_-_f_i_l_e
